Record peak, anonymous and swapped memory in get-stats.py

performance.json records each tracked process's RSS once, at the end of
the job, after memory pressure has swapped much of it out. Also record
peak RSS, anonymous RSS and swap from /proc/PID/status, which is world
readable, and the node's swap counters from /proc/vmstat.

The end-of-job RSS of privsep daemons, which the script already tracks
by default, understates them by a factor of five or more on swapping
nodes, and swap traffic is what slows those nodes down.

Prompt: Mikal asked for CI telemetry that shows how much memory privsep
daemons use, so that fixes can be landed one at a time and measured.

